======================================================================================================================
A.  IS THE ISOLATED BRANCH LEGITIMATE?  external field vs internal field, satellite by satellite
======================================================================================================================
  MOND's external-field effect is not optional: the isolated deep-MOND relation g = sqrt(g_N a0) holds only
  where the system's OWN field dominates the field it is falling in.  The physical criterion is
  g_ext vs g_int, not 'whichever formula returns the larger number'.  Milky Way field taken as v_c^2/d with
  v_c = 200 km/s, exactly as g03 and f09 do.

  system         g_N/a0  g_int/a0  g_ext/a0 g_ext/g_int                 regime    g03 branch
  Draco          0.0088    0.0940    0.1822        1.94     EXTERNAL-dominated      isolated
  Sculptor       0.0428    0.2068    0.1610        0.78     internal-dominated      isolated
  Fornax         0.1271    0.3564    0.0942        0.26     internal-dominated           EFE
  Carina         0.0091    0.0952    0.1319        1.39     EXTERNAL-dominated      isolated
  Sextans        0.0014    0.0368    0.1610        4.37     EXTERNAL-dominated      isolated
  Leo I          0.1300    0.3606    0.0545        0.15     internal-dominated           EFE
  Leo II         0.0356    0.1886    0.0594        0.32     internal-dominated      isolated
  Ursa Minor     0.0132    0.1148    0.1822        1.59     EXTERNAL-dominated      isolated
  [FAIL] V1 (THE BRANCH CRITERION IS NOT PHYSICAL) g03 assigns the external-field branch by max(g_iso, g_efe). If that rule tracked the physics, the objects it labels 'EFE' would be the externally dominated ones. It must agree with the physical criterion g_ext > g_int on all eight objects   (it agrees on NONE of the four externally dominated objects and is inverted on the two it does flag. Draco, Carina, Sextans and Ursa Minor sit in an external field 1.4 to 4.4 times their own internal MOND field and are given the ISOLATED branch; Fornax and Leo I, the two LEAST externally dominated objects (g_ext/g_int = 0.26 and 0.15), are the only two given the EFE branch. max() picks the larger number, and for high-g_N objects the quasi-Newtonian formula beats the deep-MOND asymptote for reasons that have nothing to do with the external field)
  [FAIL] V2 (HOW MANY OBJECTS ARE MISTREATED) at most one or two of the eight may be externally dominated for the isolated deep-MOND asymptote to be a defensible default across the sample   (4 of 8 are externally dominated (g_ext > g_int), and every one of them is put on the isolated branch. Sextans is the extreme case at g_ext/g_int = 4.37)

