B.  INDEPENDENT REPRODUCTION of g03's headline number, with the EXACT permutation null (all 8! orderings)
======================================================================================================================
  canonical  a0 = 9.36e-11: Spearman rho = +0.6667, Pearson = +0.6666, EXACT two-sided p = 0.0831 (1.73 sigma)
  alt        a0 = 1.13e-10: Spearman rho = +0.6667, Pearson = +0.6681, EXACT two-sided p = 0.0831 (1.73 sigma)
  g03 reported rho = +0.667 / p = 0.0820 (canonical) and +0.667 / 0.0822 (alt) from 50000 permutations.
  The exact null gives p = 0.0831; g03's Monte Carlo p is correct to its own precision.
  Achievable rho values at N=8 near the observed one: [0.5952, 0.619, 0.6429, 0.6667, 0.6905, 0.7143, 0.7381]
  [PASS] V3 (ARITHMETIC REPRODUCTION) g03's headline rho and p must reproduce independently on both footings   (rho = +0.6667 (canonical) and +0.6667 (alt), exact p = 0.0831 = 1.73 sigma. The arithmetic in g03 is sound and the 1.74 sigma is honest. Note the two footings return rho identical to 12 decimal places: a rank statistic is nearly a0-blind here by construction, so 'confirmed on both footings' carries no independent information)

