  [FAIL] V4 (THE REFUTATION) the correlation must not depend on a non-physical branch rule. Treating the external field consistently for every satellite -- by any of the three prescriptions that do so -- must leave the correlation materially above the script's own Newtonian mutation control   (self-consistent QUMOND external field gives rho = +0.429, exact p = 0.299 = 1.04 sigma, landing EXACTLY on g03's own Newtonian mutation control (+0.429), which g03's check A6 already marks FAIL. The pure quasi-Newtonian prescription gives the same +0.429 and the smooth (g_N+g_ext) one gives +0.357, i.e. every external-field-consistent prescription lands AT OR BELOW the Newtonian control. The headline +0.667 appears only in the three prescriptions that apply the isolated deep-MOND form to externally dominated satellites. Sextans' residual moves by +0.88 dex, Draco's by +0.53 dex -- these are not rounding corrections)
  [FAIL] V5 (IS THE DIFFERENCE ITSELF SIGNIFICANT?) verifying the refutation as hard as the claim: the drop from +0.667 to +0.429 must itself be larger than the noise floor at N=8, or neither number means anything   (the drop is 0.238 against a null sd of 0.378 at N=8, i.e. 0.63 sd. It is NOT resolvable. This cuts BOTH ways and is the honest reading: +0.667 and +0.429 are the same number at this sample size, so the claim is not that the correlation is refuted to be zero -- it is that NO prescription in the sweep produces a correlation distinguishable from the null, and the one that was quoted is the most favourable member of a family whose spread exceeds its own signal)

======================================================================================================================
D.  THE PHYSICS OF THE OBSERVABLE AND OF THE VARIABLE
======================================================================================================================
  all eight sit at g_N/a0 = 0.0014 to 0.1300: deep-MOND, where Milgrom's virial relation
  has the SAME form in modified inertia and in AQUAL/QUMOND, irrespective of the mass distribution.
  g03's own check A13 states this and marks it FAIL. It is correct, and it is fatal to the claim's clause.
  [FAIL] V6 (THE CLAIM'S INTERPRETIVE CLAUSE HAS NO CONTENT) for the phrase 'in the sense a trajectory-dependent modification would suggest' to be meaningful, modified inertia must predict the SIGN of this correlation. Modified inertia is a class with no unique prediction, and on a global deep-MOND virial observable the two arms are proven to agree at leading order   (no sign is predicted, which is why g03 correctly used a TWO-SIDED permutation test -- a two-sided test is the formal admission that rho = -0.667 would have been equally 'the sense modified inertia suggests'. The sign clause is post-hoc. g03's own docstring says 'MODIFIED INERTIA DOES NOT PREDICT THE SIGN', and its VERDICT block then says 'the sign is the one a trajectory-dependent modification would suggest'. Those two sentences are in the same file and cannot both stand; the claim as handed to the verifier inherits the second)
  [FAIL] V7 (WRONG ANISOTROPY) the correlating variable must be the orbit-shape quantity a trajectory-dependent modification keys on, namely the radial anisotropy beta_r = 1 - sigma_t^2/sigma_r^2 that distinguishes circular from eccentric orbits   (it is not. Hayashi+2020 define beta_z = 1 - <u_z^2>/<u_R^2> in CYLINDRICAL coordinates (verified against the paper), which measures the flattening of the velocity ellipsoid in the meridional plane, and they state 'there are obvious degeneracies between b_halo-rho_0 and Q-beta_z' where Q is the halo AXIS RATIO. beta_z is entangled with a shape parameter of the system, and there is no monotone map from beta_z to orbital eccentricity: tangential orbits confined near a plane raise beta_z exactly as in-plane radial orbits do. This also breaks g03's substitution test A9, which swaps in Vitral+2024's beta_B -- a SPHERICAL radial anisotropy, a different physical quantity from the beta_z it replaces)

