======================================================================================================================
  canonical  LVD max()  rho = +0.548, exact p = 0.1710 (1.37 sigma);  LVD self-consistent rho = +0.500 (1.24 sigma);  r(LVD, g03) = +0.955
  alt        LVD max()  rho = +0.548, exact p = 0.1710 (1.37 sigma);  LVD self-consistent rho = +0.500 (1.24 sigma);  r(LVD, g03) = +0.954
  [FAIL] V8 (THE CORROBORATION IS NOT INDEPENDENT AND IS WEAKER THAN QUOTED) the Local Volume Database rerun is offered as independent support at rho = +0.548. It must be an independent measurement and must reach the claimed strength   (the two residual vectors correlate at r = +0.955 (g03's own A4 reports +0.955): it is the same eight objects with slightly different structural inputs and the SAME eight anisotropies, so it re-tests the structural table and nothing else. Its rho = +0.548 is exact p = 0.171 = 1.37 sigma, not 1.74)

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT OF THE ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION
======================================================================================================================
  THE ARITHMETIC IS SOUND.  rho = +0.667 and p = 0.082 reproduce independently on both footings, and the
  exact 8! permutation null confirms p = 0.0831 = 1.73 sigma. The literature values were checked
  against Hayashi+2020 and all eight match, error bars included. g03 is an honest file: 10 of its 13 checks
  FAIL and its own A6, A7, A8, A9 and A13 already say most of what follows.

  THE CLAIM IS REFUTED ON THE PHYSICS, IN THREE PLACES:
  1. THE EXTERNAL FIELD.  g_pred = max(g_iso, g_efe) is not a physical criterion. Four of the eight dwarfs
     sit in a Milky Way field 1.4 to 4.4 times their own internal MOND field, and all four are given the
     ISOLATED deep-MOND asymptote; the only two given the external-field branch are the two LEAST externally
     dominated. Treating the external field consistently drops rho to +0.429 -- exactly g03's own
     Newtonian mutation control (+0.429), which A6 already marks FAIL. The excess of the headline number
     over the null control is produced by the branch rule, not by the data. This is the repository's own
     listed bug pattern: a residual whose value tracks a branch of one's own prescription.
  2. THE OBSERVABLE.  A global 3 sigma^2/R virial residual is the one observable on which Milgrom proved the
     two arms AGREE in the deep-MOND limit, and all eight dwarfs are deep-MOND. Modified inertia is a class
     and predicts no sign, so 'in the sense modified inertia would suggest' is post-hoc -- the two-sided test
     g03 correctly ran is the formal admission that rho = -0.667 would have read the same way.
  3. THE VARIABLE.  beta_z is a CYLINDRICAL vertical-to-radial ellipsoid ratio degenerate with the halo axis
     ratio Q, not the radial anisotropy that distinguishes circular from eccentric orbits. It is a shape
     parameter of the fit, not a trajectory parameter.

  AND HONESTLY, AGAINST MY OWN ATTACK: the drop from +0.667 to +0.429 is 0.63 null-sd and is NOT itself
  resolvable at N = 8. The correct statement is not 'the correlation is zero'. It is that every member of
  the prescription family lies inside the null, the family's spread exceeds its own signal, and the number
  that was quoted is the most favourable member. Nothing here says the framework fails these dwarfs; the
  self-consistent prescription that kills the correlation also enlarges the residuals, and that is a
  different question this file does not adjudicate.

  WHAT WOULD MAKE THE TEST REAL, beyond g03's own list: the residual must be recomputed with the external
  field treated self-consistently for every satellite, and the anisotropy must be a RADIAL beta_r rather
  than a cylindrical beta_z -- and an actual modified-inertia theory must be named that predicts a sign.

